# tools/ales_tone_witness.rish — a tone control: a one-pole filter that shapes a clip's brightness (ALES40).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES40.
# Design read: active-designing/20260814-160501_fill-ales40-lotus-tone-control.md
# Stands on: lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2) — the Clip it filters and the saturation it reuses (timeline.saturate).
#
# lotus/tone.rye opens the first frequency-shaping gesture: a one-pole low-pass that softens a harsh take (rolls off treble)
# and its exact high-pass complement that thins a boomy one (cuts bass). The selftest proves: silence stays silence; the
# identity coefficient (num = den) passes the low-pass through and high-passes to silence; a constant input low-passes
# MONOTONICALLY toward the input, never exceeding it, and settles to it EXACTLY (the crux — direct current reached, not merely
# approached); the high-pass reconstructs (low_pass + high_pass = x) and removes direct current; a transient SATURATES rather
# than wraps; a zero/negative/oversize coefficient refuses BadCoeff; an out-of-range span refuses BadRange leaving the clip
# untouched. Purely local — no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no real sample rate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_tone_witness.rish

say "ales-tone: Language EN — ALES40 opens the first filter: a one-pole low-pass that softens a harsh take and a high-pass that thins a boomy one — tone, the shaping gain and fade cannot do."
say "ales-tone: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: a recursive filter reaches a constant input EXACTLY and never overshoots (monotone convergence — the low-pass character), and the high-pass is the exact complement (low_pass + high_pass = x) that removes direct current."
say "ales-tone: Lens TAME — bounded Clip, u32 span, i16 samples, full i64 filter state so no fractional information is lost; a forced unit step guarantees exact direct current; the high-pass difference saturates (timeline.saturate) rather than wraps; an illegal coefficient refuses BadCoeff and an out-of-range span BadRange, each before a write; siloed to lotus/, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no sample rate."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/tone"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/tone.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-tone: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/tone.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-tone: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-tone: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-tone' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-tone: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-tone line"

say "ales-tone: GREEN — a one-pole tone control shapes a clip's brightness on integer PCM, reaching direct current exactly and saturating rather than wrapping. The next Lotus rung can sum a low-pass and a high-pass into a two-band shelf, or carry the filter state across a re-berthed span."
